## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1646217

# The data layer. Everything the player sees lives in Family_UI.
#
# The icon is the one the minimap button and the broker bars already use, and the path is
# Family_UI's on purpose: one mark for one addon, and a second copy of a 64x64 file is a
# second thing to forget when the first is redrawn. The two ship together and always have,
# so the file is on disk whenever this line is read. tests/Harness.lua checks that this path
# and the ICON constant in Family_UI/Broker.lua still name the same file.
#
# **The field is honoured**, measured in play on 2026-09-04: both rows draw the mark where
# they drew a red question mark. IconTexture was added for the addon list in 10.1.0 and all
# three pinned clients are built on engines later than that, which was the reason to expect
# it; the screenshot is why it is written here as a fact. A texture path is the thing the
# client accepts without ever saying whether it found anything (HANDOFF section 2), so the
# list itself is the only place that answer was ever going to come from.
#
# The interface numbers are major*10000 + minor*100 + patch, for Era 1.15.9, Anniversary
# 2.5.6 and Mists 5.5.4. Anniversary reported 20506 for itself in game, which is what the
# other two are computed the same way as. Bump them when the clients are patched.
#
# The multi-value form is accepted on these clients. If a future one refuses it, the fix is
# to split this file into Family_Vanilla.toc / Family_TBC.toc / Family_Mists.toc, each
# listing the same files.

# Fetched at package time rather than committed (.pkgmeta), so these files are absent from a
# git clone and present in a release. A file the client cannot find is skipped, which is
# exactly the behaviour wanted: Family works without them and says which it found.
Libs\LibStub\LibStub.lua
Libs\LibSerialize\LibSerialize.lua
Libs\LibDeflate\LibDeflate.lua

